# Source: https://github.com/hoffmangroup/segway/issues/22
#   https://genome.ucsc.edu/goldenPath/help/bigBed.html
# Symptom: first blockSize is 0, and the last block runs past chromEnd
#   (blockStarts[-1] + blockSizes[-1] = 7999 + 2000 = 9999, span = 8000).
#   bedToBigBed rejects on the zero-size block; biovalid rejects on the
#   span mismatch per hts-specs §1.9 (last block must end at chromEnd).
#   The pathology arises from Segway/segmentation tools that emit 0-origin
#   block offsets instead of sizes.
chr1	0	8000	seg001	1000	.	0	8000	217,95,2	3	0,2000,2000	0,4000,7999
